// killer.yarn

title: KillerConfession
//setting: interrogation_room
---
Bolton: We found your prints on the saxophone.

Bolton: There's already enough evidence to put you away for a long time.

Bolton: I suggest you tell us what happened.

Killer: ...I caught them together. Her and him. I thought she was staying late for rehearsal.

Bolton: Him being the saxophone player.

Killer: Was. Yeah.

Killer: I didn't go there to do anything. I just wanted to see her.

Bolton: But you did do something. Eventually.

Killer: Not that night. I just left.

Killer: I kept thinking about it. Couldn't sleep. Couldn't play. Just kept seeing them.

Bolton: The makeup wipes.

Killer: ...

Bolton: How'd you get the poison into her makeup wipes?

Killer: Does it matter?

Bolton: It does.

Killer: ...I know a guy. That's all I'll say about that.

Bolton: And the saxophone player?

Killer: He didn't even feel bad about it. I could tell. Just kept showing up to rehearsal like nothing happened.

Killer: Told him I wanted to celebrate with him after the show.

Bolton: And after the show.

Killer: He was alone in the greenroom.

Killer: I was angry, have you ever been heartbroken like that?

Bolton: ...

Killer: I know what I did.

Bolton: Yeah.

Killer: Is she...

Bolton: She didn't make it.

Killer: Figures.

You to Gray from outside of the interrogation room

You: All's in a day work huh?

Gray: Suppose so, nice work out there finding the keys and the makeup wipes.

You: Knew you'd eventually come around to liking me.

Gray: Slow your roll I tolerate you at best.

THE END.
<<ending("good")>>
===